abstract: >-
  AL-MIZAN is a complete quantum emulator implemented in pure Python with zero external dependencies,
  unifying state vector simulation (up to 16 qubits), density matrix evolution (up to 8 qubits),
  Steane [[7,1,3]] quantum error correction, zero-noise extrapolation (Richardson), and pedagogical
  GDSII layout generation. It provides sealed SHA-256 mathematical certificates for bounded verifications:
  Point Square Conjecture (PC-1..PC-6 verified by exhaustion on the declared finite domain), Turing theorem on the Riemann strip <= 100
  (29 zeros certified via interval arithmetic), and BSD verification on named elliptic curves.
  A numerical-agreement criterion (EQ-DSI-01..06) decides whether a closed form offered for a measured
  constant is derived or merely coincidental: it reproduces (79 + 48*sqrt(2) + 42*sqrt(3) + 3*sqrt(6))/31104
  to 1.42e-13, scores it at z = 0.5983879635182564 against CODATA 2022, and enumerates all 40,959,999
  forms a + b*sqrt(2) + c*sqrt(3) + d*sqrt(6) with n <= 31104, where the examined form ranks 47th of 82 at
  0.6 sigma and the best coincidence in the retained window is 108 times closer. The verdict is
  bounded to the public text examined and carries no judgment of intent.
  QPU_DISTANT re-reads one already-executed run on a distant quantum processor (job dbpkmr0ou4as73ctrm80
  on ibm_marrakesh, 256 shots on the physical support [0,1], 600 units): it recomputes the outcome
  counters from the provider result table (00 = 126, 01 = 22, 11 = 108, sum 256, so 10 = 0), reports the
  even-parity rate 0.9140625 = 234/256, and confronts it with two derived bounds - the machine median
  bound 0.9258965 is not met (-0.676 sigma) while the real-support bound 0.9114310 is met (+0.150 sigma);
  the 22-vs-0 asymmetry of the two weight-one words rejects the equiprobability null hypothesis at
  p = 4.77e-07 under an exact integer Binom(22, 1/2). The module runs no qubit, tests no AL-MIZAN
  equation and bounds only what a distant execution allows to be written.
  GOULETS bounds the publication bottlenecks measured on this workspace: 23 videos counted, longest 30 s
  against a declared 900 s threshold (870 s of margin), a 99-per-day published quota against a 10-per-day
  ceiling actually observed (ratio 9.9), a measured cadence of 1.3529 per day, 78 files and 1432.543 s in
  stock, 35434115072 free bytes out of 252841029632 (14.01 percent). Four dated, falsifiable bounds - no
  ceiling is claimed to have been lifted.
  Strict honesty constraints: every artifact carries its computational bound, no open millennium problem
  is claimed as solved. Developed by M. Ahmed EL BAHLOUL under the IMAM8MAHDI initiative.
